**[Critical]** `disabled` is hardcoded to `false` in ChatPane's composer footer, while the adjacent `ChatEditor` (line 729) receives `disabled={approvalActive}` and App.tsx's main-view footer receives the computed `isDisabled`. — Failure scenario: In split-view, when `approvalActive` is `true` (a tool approval is pending), the ChatEditor is correctly disabled but the custom composer footer receives `disabled: false`. A consumer rendering interactive controls (buttons, toggles) gated on `disabled` would leave them active while the composer is locked — inconsistent with App.tsx where both controls receive the same state.

```suggestion
            disabled={approvalActive}
            isRunning={isResponding}
            currentMode={connection.currentMode ?? 'default'}
```

<details><summary>中文说明</summary>

**[Critical]** ChatPane 中输入框 footer 的 `disabled` 被硬编码为 `false`，但相邻的 `ChatEditor`（第 729 行）接收 `disabled={approvalActive}`，App.tsx 主视图的 footer 接收计算后的 `isDisabled`。—— 失败场景：在分屏模式下，当 `approvalActive` 为 `true`（工具审批待处理时），ChatEditor 被正确禁用，但自定义输入框 footer 收到的 `disabled` 仍为 `false`。如果宿主在 footer 中渲染了基于 `disabled` 控制交互的元素（按钮、开关），这些元素会在输入框被锁定时保持可操作——与 App.tsx 中两个控件接收相同状态的行为不一致。

</details>

_— qwen3.7-max via Qwen Code /review_

